      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242849",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/0e/0e750c9fcead6818f0a185ef722a024f9ba18a6ed11d893b724b80fdfb405a89.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a circle $C$ of radius $\\frac{1}{2}$ centered at $A(3, 2)$ and the unit circle $U$ centered at the origin $O$. Prove that $C$ is similar to $U$.\n\nTo prove that $C$ is similar to $U$, we construct a sequence of similarity transformations that map $C$ onto $U$.\n\nFirst, a translation of\n{{field-1}}\nand\n{{field-2}}\nmaps the circle $C$ onto the circle $C^{\u2032}$ with\n{{field-3}}."
